I intend to put some sort of license here, but i haven't decided which one. In the interim, here is are two lists.

You are allowed to:
Download the source code files
View the source code files
Compile the source into executable code using the Warudo Playground environment.
Use that compiled code with Warudo to make cool-looking stuff.

You may not:
Remove any SPDX tags, or other copyright or attribution notices.
Distribute the compiled form of the source code files
Distribute any modified version of the source code files
Claim to have written any of the files, or otherwise misrepresent their authorship.
Submit any portion of the source code to any Large Language Model, Artificial Intelligence, or other Machine Learning system.
Redistribute the files, modified or unmodified, either as source code or as  executable object code.

The GitHub Terms of Service may grant you certain rights. The restrictions above are not intended to affect those rights.
